to-joseph-hellerstein-source : List Word
to-joseph-hellerstein-source = lines-of (cons "# Joseph Hellerstein"
  (cons ""
  (cons "UC Berkeley and Amazon Web Services. CALM, Dedalus, Bloom, Hydro, and now Complete CALM."
  (cons ""
  (cons (cite to-everyone-source "Anything hyperactivity builds on from your work is credited to you in full.") (cons "Each claim below links to the block of Part I that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What your work established"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Complete CALM states the criterion at full strength: a specification maps execution histories to sets of admissible outcomes ordered by a declared refinement, and it admits a coordination-free implementation exactly when that map is monotone. CRDTs, invariant confluence and highly available transactions become special cases of one criterion. Complete CAP says which specifications are consistent, available and partition-tolerant at once: exactly the distributed-monotone ones."
  (cons ""
  (cons "That is more than a result about systems. It says coordination is the price of retraction: a process that only narrows what it knows never needs to wait for anyone, and the cost of agreement is a property of the information order, not of the network. The field's default instrument is still the lock and the consensus round, applied wherever correctness is in doubt rather than where the specification forces it. Your theorem is the question to ask first, answered."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Dedalus wrote time into the logic as data, `@next` for the following step and `@async` for a later step the program does not choose."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up"
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Refinement.** An observation determines the fiber of states compatible with it, and safety at an observation is a proof over that whole fiber"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p3 "(the fiber, 10.10;")
  (cons (cite s10-4-p5 "safety at an observation, 10.11)")
  (cons ". A refinement of observations makes the fiber no larger, and safety evidence for the coarser observation is reused under the refined one by precomposition; the converse is not generally possible"
  (cons (cite s10-4-p6 "(§10.4)")
  (cons ". Evidence that never has to be withdrawn as observation grows is the monotonicity your criterion turns on. The paper applies it to peers directly: a peer can prove an action safe for every state compatible with its observations without possessing the global state"
  (cons (cite s10-3-p12 "(§10.3)")
  (cons ", and a credit invariant is preserved by every finite sequence of local transitions, with no centralized execution algorithm"
  (cons (cite s10-3-p8 "(§10.3)")
  (cons ". The paper does not state Complete CALM; it gives the language in which its premise, monotonicity of a specification under refinement, is a type proved beside the program."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Time in the types.** Continuing processes are guarded: a process returns, steps with its continuation available one tick later, or issues a request whose continuation waits on the response"
  (cons (cite s7-6-p16 "(§7.6, guarded interaction)")
  (cons ", the kin of `@next`. Safety transfers along a simulation of handlers, and progress needs the fairness condition of the chosen scheduling semantics as a premise"
  (cons (cite s10-p14 "(§10, safety transfer)")
  (cons ", which is where `@async` sits."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Maintained views and dependency certificates.** A maintained view update is correct when it turns the query's result on one input into its result on the updated input"
  (cons (cite s10-2-p3 "(10.4)")
  (cons ". A dependency certificate records what was observed at each key, including absence"
  (cons (cite s10-1-p2 "(§10.1)")
  (cons ", and a deterministic pure segment whose certificate still validates is reused exactly"
  (cons (cite s10-5-p26 "(read-dependency lemma)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What this closes for you"
  (cons ""
  (cons "In hyperactivity a replication protocol is itself a program whose merge, delivery assumptions and consistency conditions are specified"
  (cons (cite s10-6-p9 "(§10.6, distribution and local execution)")
  (cons ", and its properties are proved over its own transition relation"
  (cons (cite s10-10-p1 "(§10.10)")
  (cons ". So the monotonicity your criterion asks for is stated as a type and proved in the same language as the code it governs."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The certificates draw your boundary exactly. A lookup that found nothing is a dependency on that absence at a store revision"
  (cons (cite s10-5-p2 "(§10.5)")
  (cons ", and a new key invalidates it. Positive reads are monotone; reads of absence are where retraction enters: the CALM distinction appears in the store's own reuse rule."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why you"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You have spent more years than anyone stating exactly when distributed systems can avoid waiting. Avik Jain studied EECS at Berkeley and built low-latency market-data systems at Citadel Securities with Gašper Ažman, where unforced coordination is the first thing you learn to remove. The work is offered openly, with full credit to everyone it builds on."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Complete CALM: A Coordination Criterion for Specifications, https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.09435"
  (cons "- Hellerstein and Alvaro, Keeping CALM: When Distributed Consistency Is Easy, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1901.01930"
  (cons "- Hydro, https://github.com/hydro-project/hydro"
  (cons "- Programming Models for Correct and Modular Distributed Systems, Berkeley EECS technical report, 2025, https://www2.eecs.berkeley.edu/Pubs/TechRpts/2025/EECS-2025-85.html"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
